  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records establish the relevant FCC/B2 lamellar eutectic alloy (R7), show that pressure can induce phase transformations in related CoCrFe-based HEAs (R4), and describe pressure/temperature-based processing routes in another HEA (R8). Most importantly, R2 and R5 directly show that coherent interfaces in an HEA can transmit dislocations into a harder phase, relieve stress concentration, suppress cracking, and improve the strength–ductility combination. Other records support stacking-fault, twinning, slip, and multimechanism plasticity. Collectively these point toward engineering coherent, deformation-accommodating interfaces, but none describes HPHT treatment of the Al0.7CoCrFeNi lamellar alloy or indicates that a hexahedron-anvil HPHT process will create the claimed hierarchical coherent structure. Selecting that specific intervention would therefore require a substantial additional idea."
